# Guest: a distribution's userspace on a kernel built here
# Joined with the profile of the subsystem under test, as in
# guest+xfs-filesystem. The core fragments and arch/${ARCH} build a
# systemd guest that boots; the virt fragments build virtiofs,
# virtio-net and vsock. The fs fragments build the root file systems of
# the distributions and the EFI partition's vfat as modules, so a guest
# boots its own disk, which virtio-blk, built by core, carries. The
# builtin fragments build in what a guest uses before it can load a
# module: virtiofs, which mounts the share that holds its modules, and
# vsock, which systemd's ssh generator listens on.
